# Tracked files that ripgrep (and every agent search tool built on it) should skip.
#
# `.gitignore` is the wrong lever here: these files must stay *tracked* — groom serves
# its assets from the wheel, and the a11y suite loads its vendored axe from disk. What
# they must not do is answer a search. Each is a single machine-generated line tens to
# hundreds of kilobytes wide, so one incidental match pastes the whole bundle into a
# reader's context and buys nothing: nobody edits minified output, and the fix always
# lands upstream in the dependency rather than here.
#
# The bar for adding a line: the file has no human-authored line breaks, or is
# machine-generated output. Anything a person would edit stays
# searchable, however large.

# Vendored browser bundles served by groom's dashboard.
groom/groom/assets/*.min.js
groom/groom/assets/*.min.css
groom/groom/assets/htm-preact.js

# The axe-core build the accessibility suite loads (552 KB on one line).
groom/tests/vendor/axe.min.js
